{
  "version": 1,
  "purpose": "Static explicit native-Web operation routing policy. This file is hand-reviewed source inventory, never generated from a running registry. Routing scope is not authorization or evidence of feature completion.",
  "inventorySources": [
    "src/shared/ipc-channels.ts: AllInvokeChannels and all separately imported channel interfaces",
    "electron/controllers/*-controller.ts: literal and helper registrations, including register(channel,...)",
    "electron/controllers/finalization-controller.ts: finalization:commit and finalization:retry outside AllInvokeChannels",
    "electron/mcp/mcp-ipc-bridge.ts: separately composed MCP registrations"
  ],
  "scopeDefinitions": {
    "global": "Single global worker owns settings/model credentials/prompts/skills/metadata/integration registry. Principal/role checks are still required.",
    "project": "Require this client's active owned project worker plus current project/session lease. Root/path parameters never grant authority.",
    "flexible": "Capability/dialog or execution lifecycle may originate before project open or inside a project. Route to the originating worker for grant/run/lease ownership, not merely whichever project is current now."
  },
  "securityRequirements": [
    "Unknown operations and web: internal helpers are denied; no prefix or registry-wide exposure.",
    "Project fs names below are authorized project-root operations, not arbitrary host filesystem APIs. Existing project session, safe-file capability and path guards must remain authoritative.",
    "Dialog and fs:grant operations must retain server-assigned caller, purpose, expiry and originating-worker bindings; flexible is not global authority.",
    "MCP lifecycle/config reload and all command/args/env configuration are administrator-limited; tool calls require assigned server/tool permissions and effect confirmation. Exposing a route alone does not enforce this.",
    "Proxy/egress/global credential administration needs role enforcement; a string routing scope cannot distinguish administrators from authors.",
    "llm generate/cancel/execution leases must stay bound to originating client/worker; saved and unsaved endpoints require egress policy and all public model responses require redaction.",
    "Cloud connect/list/clear operate on the global credential/binding store; view/confirm/backup need project authority. Project-worker backup/confirm/restore must delegate global metadata writes to the single writer rather than racing shared JSON stores.",
    "Cloud restore/cancel and project archive/dialog flows require originating-worker routing and operation ownership. Do not assume a flexible call's current project resolves its grant/operation owner.",
    "Fixed external-resource operations are browser-navigation replacements only, not server shell/openExternal capabilities.",
    "Source-admission-only mutators intentionally rejected by the existing domain remain rejected; allowlisting does not waive their admission gate."
  ],
  "excluded": {
    "window:minimize": "Desktop window operation; browser owns its window.",
    "window:toggle-maximize": "Desktop window operation; product focus mode is separate.",
    "window:close": "Desktop close operation; never close the server through RPC.",
    "window:resolve-close": "Desktop close protocol; browser dirty/unload flow replaces it.",
    "update:get-state": "Desktop updater lifecycle; browser uses deployment-managed version/capability projection.",
    "update:check": "Desktop release check is not Web deployment management.",
    "update:download": "No desktop installer download on server.",
    "update:open-release": "Use a fixed browser link instead of desktop shell.",
    "update:defer-reminder": "Desktop reminder state; replace through Web capability UI if needed.",
    "update:quit-and-install": "Never install binaries or restart service through ordinary browser RPC.",
    "project:smoke-open-request": "Desktop/test-only host path hook.",
    "project:smoke-open-confirm": "Desktop/test-only host marker hook.",
    "mcp:get-config-path": "Host configuration path must not be exposed to ordinary authors; use sanitized admin-managed capability metadata."
  },
